## Page 3 — Brokers (`/brokers`)

### Messaging Strategy

**Primary emotion to address:** Respect for their time and expertise. Brokers are professionals. They don't want a pitch — they want to understand quickly whether Ownly fits their workflow.

**Critical message:** Ownly is not competing with brokers. Ownly is a presentation and distribution tool that makes their listings better. The platform does not take a success fee from broker-submitted deals.

**Tone:** Peer-to-peer. Direct. No fluff. Assume they know M&A.

**Key anxiety to address:** "Is this going to compete with me for clients?" Answer: No.

### Sections

#### 1. Hero

**H1:**
> Better listings. More qualified enquiries.

**Subheadline:**
> Ownly gives your deals a structured home — a professional deal page that buyers can evaluate properly. You keep the client relationship. We handle presentation and inbound.

**CTA:** `List your first deal free →`  
**Secondary CTA:** `Talk to us →` (email link or contact form)

---

